      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A study of the immune and fibrinolytic systems of the body in 216 patients with different clinical forms of atherosclerosis (exertion and rest stenocardia, arrhythmias, atherosclerotic hypertension), chronic obstructive bronchitis revealed that the antiatherogenous effect of chronic obstructive bronchitis is predetermined on the one side by an increased function of the monocytic-macrophagal link of immunity and on the other by activation of the fibrinolysis system."},
